{"h":3395,"w":2400,"lines":[{"w":0.069958845774332645,"x":0.7716049391467531,"t":"1718867188","h":0.008720930389296444,"c":0.30000001192092896,"y":0.046511627815394085},{"h":0.014128817545932315,"y":0.053255358641868034,"c":1,"t":"Test 1","x":0.11705427999468544,"w":0.058072509765625016},{"c":1,"y":0.094220416640889537,"t":"READING","x":0.44437521112505673,"w":0.12771048227945958,"h":0.017954515203289501},{"c":1,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","x":0.11728395059070985,"w":0.28600822448730473,"y":0.15253239080129843,"h":0.014723203769140158},{"w":0.76155532836914064,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","y":0.18566275805027488,"c":1,"x":0.11717408719776737,"h":0.020467385245998226},{"t":"Passage 1 below.","x":0.11728394985675578,"y":0.2034746760602486,"w":0.15843621571858724,"c":1,"h":0.016002067547945309},{"y":0.24705535911250132,"t":"The development of the London underground railway","w":0.74279836018880208,"h":0.020386501532420942,"x":0.13580246588583841,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.74485595703124985,"t":"In the first half of the 1800s, London's population grew at an astonishing rate, and the central","x":0.11522634235899593,"y":0.28474676068355675,"h":0.016195524146054074},{"w":0.71193415323893228,"h":0.014534882858869502,"x":0.11728394656297572,"t":"area became increasingly congested. In addition, the expansion of the overground railway","c":1,"y":0.30087209321203812},{"x":0.11522634677239324,"w":0.77160491943359366,"y":0.31831395334239154,"t":"network resulted in more and more passengers arriving in the capital. However, in 1846, a Royal","h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1},{"h":0.017667844522968101,"y":0.33421672557003013,"w":0.72016459147135414,"t":"Commission decided that the railways should not be allowed to enter the City, the capital's","c":1,"x":0.11728395930517867},{"y":0.35029069754161446,"x":0.11728394643655284,"w":0.74897120157877617,"c":1,"t":"historic and business centre. The result was that the overground railway stations formed a ring","h":0.014550291607320798},{"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"w":0.78189300537109385,"y":0.36773255798815552,"x":0.11728394988353016,"t":"around the City. The area within consisted of poorly built, overcrowded slums and the streets were"},{"t":"full of horse-drawn traffic. Crossing the City became a nightmare. It could take an hour and a half","x":0.11522634488088347,"c":1,"y":0.38515901084696824,"w":0.78395060221354174,"h":0.01455029160732102},{"y":0.40106007061628712,"t":"to travel 8 km by horse-drawn carriage or bus. Numerous schemes were proposed to resolve these","x":0.11522633670712783,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"w":0.78189300537109385},{"t":"problems, but few succeeded.","x":0.11522634332339488,"w":0.23868311564127603,"c":1,"y":0.41860465102490796,"h":0.014552004064912749},{"x":0.11522633702929141,"y":0.45053003552947457,"t":"Amongst the most vocal advocates for a solution to London's traffic problems was Charles","w":0.72427983601888024,"c":1,"h":0.014723203769140047},{"h":0.016781471643346757,"c":1,"x":0.11518520336390016,"w":0.74287760416666671,"t":"Pearson, who worked as a solicitor for the City of London. He saw both social and economic","y":0.46652828629309395},{"y":0.4840116277742611,"c":1,"t":"advantages in building an underground railway that would link the overground railway stations","x":0.11728396275673182,"w":0.75308639526367194,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"h":0.01453488398216074,"y":0.5014534882394307,"w":0.77572016398111976,"t":"together and clear London slums at the same time. His idea was to relocate the poor workers who","x":0.11522633766312348,"c":1},{"w":0.74897120157877595,"y":0.51737338056309201,"c":1,"h":0.014723203769140158,"x":0.11522633326208127,"t":"lived in the inner-city slums to newly constructed suburbs, and to provide cheap rail travel for"},{"x":0.11728396185707624,"w":0.7592592366536457,"c":1,"h":0.014567411690072807,"t":"them to get to work. Pearson's ideas gained support amongst some businessmen and in 1851 he","y":0.53343023242449616},{"w":0.77572016398111976,"c":1,"x":0.1152263376518988,"y":0.55087209287717109,"t":"submitted a plan to Parliament. It was rejected, but coincided with a proposal from another group","h":0.01598837238037687},{"x":0.11522632936288464,"y":0.56684334488044552,"w":0.49794240315755206,"c":1,"h":0.016005492463128657,"t":"for an underground connecting line, which Parliament passed."},{"h":0.014550291607320909,"t":"The two groups merged and established the Metropolitan Railway Company in August 1854. The","y":0.6002906975418123,"x":0.11728394266269523,"w":0.77366256713867188,"c":1},{"w":0.76337448120117191,"x":0.11522633961361435,"t":"company's plan was to construct an underground railway line from the Great Western Railway's","y":0.61627906962008105,"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1},{"w":0.7633744812011718,"x":0.11522633953898681,"y":0.63368669049598447,"t":"(GWR) station at Paddington to the edge of the City at Farringdon Street - a distance of almost","c":1,"h":0.014569123586018806},{"t":"5 km. The organisation had difficulty in raising the funding for such a radical and expensive","y":0.64958775026580318,"w":0.73456792195638021,"x":0.11522632697170858,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1},{"y":0.66569767463671881,"h":0.015988371257085632,"t":"scheme, not least because of the critical articles printed by the press. Objectors argued that the","x":0.11522635556731056,"c":1,"w":0.75514399210611982},{"t":"tunnels would collapse under the weight of traffic overhead, buildings would be shaken and","h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"x":0.11522632792506594,"y":0.68313953473692135,"w":0.72839508056640623},{"y":0.69905771516466098,"c":1,"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.11728395087183534,"t":"passengers would be poisoned by the emissions from the train engines. However, Pearson and his","w":0.77572016398111987},{"y":0.71643109567161367,"w":0.15020575205485026,"h":0.013250883392226132,"x":0.11728395617422095,"t":"partners persisted.","c":1},{"h":0.015929924163998077,"y":0.74813809333361381,"w":0.72233032226562499,"t":"The GWR, aware that the new line would finally enable them to run trains into the heart of","c":1,"x":0.11928900500744134},{"h":0.016195524146054185,"y":0.76590106019878856,"t":"the City, invested almost £250,000 in the scheme. Eventually, over a five-year period, f1m","w":0.72016459147135414,"c":1,"x":0.1152263461373939},{"w":0.70781890869140629,"x":0.11934157445108316,"y":0.78197674404389561,"c":1,"h":0.014548579711374909,"t":"was raised. The chosen route ran beneath existing main roads to minimise the expense of"},{"y":0.8677325578911671,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"w":0.024691357612609877,"t":"16","x":0.11728395082332468},{"t":"IELTSXpress.com","c":1,"x":0.66991655033568553,"w":0.30612678527832038,"h":0.03375352650564889,"y":0.95314993796778535}]}